{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods","id":662321,"title":"Making Wolf-Bloods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T16:03:32-07:00","id":662321,"title":"Making Wolf-Bloods","content":"So in the second edition of Werewolf the Forsaken dramatically failing a Lunacy save makes that character wolf-blooded, automatically, in a month or less? I have found no in-game justification for this. Why does this happen?<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one who thinks this is abuseable, given that with new rules players can choose to botch a roll they already failed? And really why would you ever choose to be panic-stricken or catatonic when you can receive permanent immunity to Lunacy and also wolf-powers?? I know the <i>character</i> doesn't know that's the choice they get but why would any player not take that option?<br /> <br /> As an alternative, what breaks if I say that in my setting humans become wolf-blooded if they survive being the target of a sacred hunt or <i>basu-im</i> after taking lethal damage? I'm cashing in on the &quot;survivors of werewolf attacks become werewolves&quot; myth here, but would that be any better than the canon rules for becoming wolf blooded you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:37:13-07:00","id":662384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods#post662321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the second edition of Werewolf the Forsaken dramatically failing a Lunacy save makes that character wolf-blooded, automatically, in a month or less? I have found no in-game justification for this. Why does this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods#post662321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I the only one who thinks this is abuseable, given that with new rules players can choose to botch a roll they already failed? And really why would you ever choose to be panic-stricken or catatonic when you can receive permanent immunity to Lunacy and also wolf-powers?? I know the <i>character</i> doesn't know that's the choice they get but why would any player not take that option?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about anyone else, but I wouldn't let players off with the consequences of failing the roll just because the dramatic failure doesn't explicitly list them. You're getting hit by lunacy hard enough to alter your very nature. If anything, you're gonna be <i>extra</i> catatonic after that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:05:04-07:00","id":662420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods#post662321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the second edition of Werewolf the Forsaken dramatically failing a Lunacy save makes that character wolf-blooded, automatically, in a month or less? I have found no in-game justification for this. Why does this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 297, under Adoptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, am I the only one who thinks this is abuseable, given that with new rules players can choose to botch a roll they already failed? And really why would you ever choose to be panic-stricken or catatonic when you can receive permanent immunity to Lunacy and also wolf-powers?? I know the <i>character</i> doesn't know that's the choice they get but why would any player not take that option? </div> </div> </div>A Storyteller can decide if that's alright or not. But since only humans can become wolf-blooded and wolf-blooded won't definitely become Uratha it's not really something you can abuse. It also requires them to fail a roll in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an alternative, what breaks if I say that in my setting humans become wolf-blooded if they survive being the target of a sacred hunt or <i>basu-im</i> after taking lethal damage? I'm cashing in on the &quot;survivors of werewolf attacks become werewolves&quot; myth here, but would that be any better than the canon rules for becoming wolf blooded you think? </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be better, it's probably something that would happen in games anyways. Though I'll point out having played the game and my character having eaten half a dozen humans with ease, the odds of someone surviving an actual hunt to the death are ridiculously slim. Targets of the hunt do get a bonus to Lunacy but they'd probably facing enough penalties and other gifts that they might get the dramatic failure anyways.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to do it for your games go for it. Though I'll point out that you don't really change what you view as abuse. A werewolf can just call a sacred hunt on a human they want to turn, inflict a point of lethal damage, and the hunt can be over. Hunts aren't always to the death, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-12-2015, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:49:43-07:00","id":662503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662420#post662420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 297, under Adoptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lunacy, possession, sexually transmitted pseudo-lychanthropy and sometimes a severe reaction to the bite of a werewolf can all create a wolf blooded where one did not exist before. Uratha who research such things have found no pattern, and the circumstances that cause this to happen can't be machinated. It just happens sometimes at random, or sometimes with a strange poetry of fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...wow that is in no way better than no explanation at all. Like I'm sorry, thank you for answering my question, and maybe people like this sort of enforced mystery but as a storyteller I don't enjoy being told that I will never know the answer to this incredibly important piece of setting fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662420#post662420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said if you want to do it for your games go for it. Though I'll point out that you don't really change what you view as abuse. A werewolf can just call a sacred hunt on a human they want to turn, inflict a point of lethal damage, and the hunt can be over. Hunts aren't always to the death, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't? I was under the decided impression that they were. Well in that case I'd be ruling that this boon only happens sometimes and only when the target survives a hunt to the death by their own power. Like to Mother Luna and Father Wolf that is just damn impressive, and Wolf-Bloodedness is one of the ways they commonly reward such heroism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:58:29-07:00","id":662507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lunacy, possession, sexually transmitted pseudo-lychanthropy and sometimes a severe reaction to the bite of a werewolf can all create a wolf blooded where one did not exist before. Uratha who research such things have found no pattern, and the circumstances that cause this to happen can't be machinated. It just happens sometimes at random, or sometimes with a strange poetry of fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...wow that is in no way better than no explanation at all. Like I'm sorry, thank you for answering my question, and maybe people like this sort of enforced mystery but as a storyteller I don't enjoy being told that I will never know the answer to this incredibly important piece of setting fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna is a mad god, if you want there to be method to her madness it's up to you as a storyteller to create it. But seeing as she's a mad god of change, actually changing people is within her wheelhouse. Also, arguably, Luna likes having more and more wolf-blooded and werewolves. There are theories scattered across books. Since werewolves have been with humanity since the beginning, breeding with them, it's possible everyone has a little wolf in them, and being so dramatically open to Lunacy might sort of provoke those ancient genes into action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't? I was under the decided impression that they were. Well in that case I'd be ruling that this boon only happens sometimes and only when the target survives a hunt to the death by their own power. Like to Mother Luna and Father Wolf that is just damn impressive, and Wolf-Bloodedness is one of the ways they commonly reward such heroism. </div> </div> </div>Well, Father Wolf is dead so he wouldn't care, but sure go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:35:54-07:00","id":662553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lunacy, possession, sexually transmitted pseudo-lychanthropy and sometimes a severe reaction to the bite of a werewolf can all create a wolf blooded where one did not exist before. Uratha who research such things have found no pattern, and the circumstances that cause this to happen can't be machinated. It just happens sometimes at random, or sometimes with a strange poetry of fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...wow that is in no way better than no explanation at all. Like I'm sorry, thank you for answering my question, and maybe people like this sort of enforced mystery but as a storyteller I don't enjoy being told that I will never know the answer to this incredibly important piece of setting fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because there is no hard answer given in the core book doesn't mean you'll never know the answer. For one thing, this way you're free to decide on any answer you like and it won't contradict canon. Besides that, there's going to be more werewolf books. I would be surprised if none of them expanded on the whens, whys, and hows of spontaneous Wolf-Blooded &quot;adoptions.&quot; I would also be surprised if there weren't canonical exceptions to any pattern that may be established in later books. That's nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T20:07:00-07:00","id":662595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't? I was under the decided impression that they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the Resolution criteria for the Siskur-Dah Condition on page 310.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T20:33:24-07:00","id":662610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I the only one who thinks this is abuseable, given that with new rules players can choose to botch a roll they already failed? And really why would you ever choose to be panic-stricken or catatonic when you can receive permanent immunity to Lunacy and also wolf-powers?? I know the <i>character</i> doesn't know that's the choice they get but why would any player not take that option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, being immune to lunacy is hardly a fail-safe against the attention of a pack if the human is deemed to be more useful 6 feet under.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lunacy, possession, sexually transmitted pseudo-lychanthropy and sometimes a severe reaction to the bite of a werewolf can all create a wolf blooded where one did not exist before. Uratha who research such things have found no pattern, and the circumstances that cause this to happen can't be machinated. It just happens sometimes at random, or sometimes with a strange poetry of fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...wow that is in no way better than no explanation at all. Like I'm sorry, thank you for answering my question, and maybe people like this sort of enforced mystery but as a storyteller I don't enjoy being told that I will never know the answer to this incredibly important piece of setting fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you create your own setting, you will, as nofather so aptly explained.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T02:22:38-07:00","id":662836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=662503#post662503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...wow that is in no way better than no explanation at all. Like I'm sorry, thank you for answering my question, and maybe people like this sort of enforced mystery but as a storyteller I don't enjoy being told that I will never know the answer to this incredibly important piece of setting fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're the ST nothing happens in your world without you creating the reason for it to happen, so that seems like an invalid complaint to me. It in fact insulates you as the ST from rules lawyering players going &quot;page XX says I can do Y&quot; and puts more, not less, control in your hands. It's a game, not a lesson in werewolf metaphysics. As far as recognizing &quot;heroism&quot;, Father Wolf is dead and Luna has no fucks to give, unless you decide otherwise in your game. This isn't Apocalypse (which I love but can get a little too grainy with explanations, sometimes) and the current set up frees you from having to mess too much with the background setting to tell the type of story or play the type of game you want, but it does require a little more prep work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:13:12-07:00","id":663566,"title":"","content":"So I ended doing some research about where werewolves come from. I was expecting to find a clear, concise answer in one of the early chapters, and was surprised when I didn't. In particular, information about what life was like before the First Change was so sparse as to be non-existent, save only for the period immediately leading into the First Change \u2014 and even there, the focus was less about what life was like before the Change and more about how life before the Change was disrupted. <br /> <br /> The closest thing to an answer to the matter came in \u201cthe First Change Chronicle\u201d, where the text carried the implicit assumption that since you're about to play through the First Change, then <i>of course</i> that means that you're going to be playing a wolf-blooded. Unless I missed something, this is the first and only time in the text where it's even <i>implied</i> that every Uratha was a wolf-blooded before her First Change. <br /> <br /> I even went looking for the Prelude section of character creation to see if <i>that</i> had anything to say about a werewolf\u2019s former life, as the Prelude has traditionally been the place where questions such as this are answered. Except that the only mention of any sort of a \u201cPrelude\u201d is the Pack Prelude \u2014 and that\u2019s only a prelude in the most general sense, as it focuses on \u201cwhat\u2019s the Pack like?\u201d rather than \u201chow did the Pack come to be?\u201d <br /> <br /> I'm assuming that much of this will be addressed by upcoming supplements such as \u201cThe Pack\u201d; but for now, it appears that we have to rely on what the developers have said in the forums and blogs. Going with that, here\u2019s what I\u2019ve gathered:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nearly all Uratha were once Wolf-Blooded. The only exception to this would be a mortal who was exposed to the spiritual energies of the werewolf\u2019s world (see \u201cAdoption\u201d and \u201cOrphans\u201d under the Wolf-Blooded) and <i>immediately</i> went through the First Change. Even there, the Uratha was <i>technically</i> wolf-blooded prior to her First Change; it\u2019s just that her time spent as a wolf-blooded was insignificant. Beyond that, the question of werewolf origins becomes a question of the lifestyles of the Wolf-Blooded. <br /> \u2022 Many Wolf-Blooded belong to Packs. My inclination would be to say that <i>most</i> do, as the Wolf-Blooded tend to be drawn to the Uratha and vice versa; but either way, a <i>common</i> setup should be that Packs predate their current rosters: that is, a frequent origin for a werewolf should be \u201cshe used to be one of our Wolf-Blooded, until she got \u2018promoted\u2019 by her First Change.\u201d (Side note: are a Pack\u2019s Wolf-Blooded bound to the Pack\u2019s Totem, or is that bond unique to the Uratha? If the former, a Pack Wolf-Blooded who undergoes the First Change should automatically become part of the Pack\u2019s hunting party, barring personality clashes that force her out; if the latter, the newly Changed werewolf should have to \u201csign up\u201d with the Pack\u2019s Totem in order to join the hunting party.)<br /> \u2022 Those Wolf-Blooded who <i>don\u2019t</i> belong to Packs still have Tells; so even if a given Uratha has no past experience with a Pack, she almost certainly has familiarity with the world of Mother Luna and Father Wolf. Or do the Wolf-Blooded <i>themselves</i> have something akin to a First Change, prior to which they're essentially indistinguishable from regular mortals? The \u201cSons of Mother Luna\u201d and \u201cDaughters of Father Wolf\u201d sections certainly imply that a Wolf-Blooded can point to a moment prior to which he had no Tell and was as vulnerable to Lunacy as anyone else. <br /> \u2022 Even if a potential Wolf-Blooded hasn't manifested a Tell, there's a good chance that he knows (or at least knows <i>of</i>) someone who has. The exception, again, is the ordinary mortal who ends up <i>becoming</i> Wolf-Blooded through exposure to the supernatural world of the werewolf, most commonly represented by botching a Lunacy test. <br /> <br /> I tend to agree with kindledRadial on one point: I don't think that botching a Lunacy test should automatically make you Wolf-Blooded. It should certainly open the door; but ultimately, becoming Wolf-Blooded should require an unknown factor that leaves it open to the Storyteller as to whether a botched Lunacy test \u201cmerely\u201d has the usual results of a botched degeneration check or if it initiates a transformation from mortal to Wolf-Blooded. In the latter case, I tend to think there's more story potential if the transformation isn't necessarily immediate, but can manifest as a gradual \u201cinfection\u201d of the soon-to-be Wolf-Blooded's being, which he has time to (attempt to) fight. <br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> like that the origins of the werewolf have largely been decoupled from Uratha mating habits: even to the extent that Wolf-Blooded gain that status as a birthright (which strikes me as an Ivory Claws notion), it's not so much the mating habits of the <i>Uratha</i> that matters as it is the mating habits of the <i>Wolf-Blooded</i>. This nicely sidesteps a number of unfortunate implications, ranging from domestic abuse to bestiality: in the former case, the fact tha the Uratha don\u2019t need to breed to produce more Wolf-Blooded means that you don't need to worry about the problematic aspects of a killing machine having intimate relations with a regular mortal; in the latter case, there's really no reason to even bring up the issue anymore: even if, say, the Predator Kings end up with Wolf-Blooded wolves in their Packs (and thus potentially introduce to WtF the concept of wolf-born werewolves), it\u2019s easy enough to say that wolves breed with wolves and humans breed with humans, and the two \u201cBreeds\u201d (to borrow a WtA term) remain separate and distinct. <br /> <br /> But more generally, how one becomes Wolf-Blooded seems to be more a matter of Mother Luna's whims than anything that can be predicted with any reliability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:16:50-07:00","id":663569,"title":"","content":"The fact that humans can be made wolf-blooded just by seeing a werewolf is a huge deal. It means that if you are a werewolf and you want to mass-produce wolf-bloods then all you have to do is chain them to the radiator and walk around in Dalu until someone botches, at which point they stop screaming at the sight of you. You can just keep doing that. No guarantee they will want to help you afterwards, but throw in some dominate gifts and now you have wolf-blooded shock troops.<br /> <br /> To draw a parallel, vampires can make as many ghouls as they like. This is a big power balance issue which is mostly solved by the fact that the Requiem is arguably one big game of &quot;murder in the dark&quot; and if you start mass producing shock troops someone is going to notice and hog-tie you to a tanning booth. But werewolves don't have that same level of paranoia or oversight. If making wolf-bloods is this easy then why doesn't everyone do it?<br /> <br /> Also, this just isn't a thing werewolves do? Like I have an infinite wellspring of love for whoever rewrote the gift list from the original Forsaken because Uratha used to be able to do everything from running faster to excreting fresh ground Columbian dark roast from their skin. You pull that last one out during game and suddenly all pretense that were are playing &quot;werewolves the tabletop&quot; is shattered. That's exactly the feeling I'm getting from being able to turn people wolf-blooded on sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 09-13-2015, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:47:41-07:00","id":663630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663569#post663569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that humans can be made wolf-blooded just by seeing a werewolf is a huge deal. It means that if you are a werewolf and you want to mass-produce wolf-bloods then all you have to do is chain them to the radiator and walk around in Dalu until someone botches, at which point they stop screaming at the sight of you. You can just keep doing that. No guarantee they will want to help you afterwards, but throw in some dominate gifts and now you have wolf-blooded shock troops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except as it said the circumstances that create it can't be machinated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To draw a parallel, vampires can make as many ghouls as they like. This is a big power balance issue which is mostly solved by the fact that the Requiem is arguably one big game of &quot;murder in the dark&quot; and if you start mass producing shock troops someone is going to notice and hog-tie you to a tanning booth. But werewolves don't have that same level of paranoia or oversight. If making wolf-bloods is this easy then why doesn't everyone do it? </div> </div> </div>Plus there's the fact that wolf-blooded are not servants the way that ghouls are. A wolf-blooded is perfectly capable of going to get silver bullets and pumping a werewolf full of them for chaining them up to a radiator and driving them insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, this just isn't a thing werewolves do? Like I have an infinite wellspring of love for whoever rewrote the gift list from the original Forsaken because Uratha used to be able to do everything from running faster to excreting fresh ground Columbian dark roast from their skin. You pull that last one out during game and suddenly all pretense that were are playing &quot;werewolves the tabletop&quot; is shattered. That's exactly the feeling I'm getting from being able to turn people wolf-blooded on sight. </div> </div> </div>You're also encouraged to avoid doing it, as it is part of the Oath of the Moon. The Herd Must Not Know. Lunacy happens, but when you go around causing it all the time you're violating the Oath of the Moon and suffering Harmony losses for it. It's also worth noting that just happening to see a werewolf isn't likely to cause a Dramatic Failure result except in the weakest of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:55:29-07:00","id":663631,"title":"","content":"The Uratha don't know that a dramatic failure on a lunacy roll can make a human into a wolf-blooded. They don't even know what a dramatic failure or a lunacy roll is. All they know is that sometimes people who come into contact with werewolves become wolf-blooded, and sometimes they don't. It makes a lot of sense that myths would arise to try to explain a common factor among spontaneous adoptions, like &quot;it only happens if the werewolf bites you&quot; or &quot;it only happens on the full moon&quot; or what have you. The truth is Luna is not so consistent as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:01:43-07:00","id":663637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663566#post663566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I missed something, this is the first and only time in the text where it's even <i>implied</i> that every Uratha was a wolf-blooded before her First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 296 all but explicitly states it: &quot;Where do Werewolves come from? Not in the grand scheme, but in the immediate, visceral, bodily sense? Short and sweet, they come from Wolf-Blooded.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, Chris and I think some of the other writers have stated that not all Werewolves are Wolf-Blooded before their First Change, so... *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:08:56-07:00","id":663638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663637#post663637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, Chris and I think some of the other writers have stated that not all Werewolves are Wolf-Blooded before their First Change, so... *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel noted that one doesn't have to spend a lot of time being a wolf-blooded. You can be a wolf-blooded from birth, or Luna can just choose you and you can enjoy being wolf-blooded for a day before your First Change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:28:29-07:00","id":663656,"title":"","content":"Because wolfbloods aren't shock troops. A ghoul is dependent on their regnant to continue to reap the benefits of their new immortality. A wolfblood turned by a werewolf is free to just walk away and continue living his life and may even resent a werewolf who intentionally tuned him. He is under no obligation to join a pack or the pack of the werewolf that turned him. They have no connection or tie or bond with said werewolf. They are no more likely to be Pure or Forsaken. I can think of certain motivations where it would make sense to mass create wolfbloods, but none of them seem very common or very sensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:39:39-07:00","id":663682,"title":"","content":"Shock troops that are quivering in a heap in the corner because you destroyed their sanity turning them into wolf-blooded aren't going to be very useful for anything other than a quick Essence refill/snack. What is being proposed is torture, not really something the Oath condones, and as been pointed out the Uratha don't have access to rulebooks telling them about botched rolls. I personally don't like metagamers at my table and if someone tried that they'd quickly find out why the Uratha have reason to fear their cousins when they gather in numbers with silver weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:13:46-07:00","id":663795,"title":"","content":"Even setting aside the personal grudges wolf-blooded might bear, I'd really hope it goes without saying why it's a bad idea to try to torture people into maybe becoming gateways to another world when extreme emotionally-resonant activity is among the fastest ways to make spirits that are both active and well-armed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:34:58-07:00","id":663799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663795#post663795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even setting aside the personal grudges wolf-blooded might bear, I'd really hope it goes without saying why it's a bad idea to try to torture people into maybe becoming gateways to another world when extreme emotionally-resonant activity is among the fastest ways to make spirits that are both active and well-armed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like something the Bale Hounds might do or a crazy Pure.<br /> <br /> I remember some of the writers saying you don't need to be a wolf blooded in order to become a full fledge werewolf. So in my games if a character gets dramatic failure+ in Lunacy, then they automatically become Uratha. But I hope future supplements can cover more on wolf blooded and First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:08:46-07:00","id":663818,"title":"","content":"Does the 2ed rulebook bring up the idea that wolf blooded (who don't have a rule book and may not understand what they are) might instead become werewolf hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:02:24-07:00","id":663879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663818#post663818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 2ed rulebook bring up the idea that wolf blooded (who don't have a rule book and may not understand what they are) might instead become werewolf hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it need to be called out specifically? Seems like common sense to me that it would happen every once in a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T01:47:24-07:00","id":664051,"title":"","content":"Page 297 under &quot;A Vigil&quot;. It is specifically called out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit; I do agree with Cha\u200brlaquin that it seems like a common sense assumption in the game, didn't want my post to be interpreted as a wise ass retort to yours C.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-14-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T02:51:54-07:00","id":664067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=663569#post663569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that humans can be made wolf-blooded just by seeing a werewolf is a huge deal. It means that if you are a werewolf and you want to mass-produce wolf-bloods then all you have to do is chain them to the radiator and walk around in Dalu until someone botches, at which point they stop screaming at the sight of you. You can just keep doing that. No guarantee they will want to help you afterwards, but throw in some dominate gifts and now you have wolf-blooded shock troops.<br /> <br /> To draw a parallel, vampires can make as many ghouls as they like. This is a big power balance issue which is mostly solved by the fact that the Requiem is arguably one big game of &quot;murder in the dark&quot; and if you start mass producing shock troops someone is going to notice and hog-tie you to a tanning booth. But werewolves don't have that same level of paranoia or oversight. If making wolf-bloods is this easy then why doesn't everyone do it?<br /> <br /> Also, this just isn't a thing werewolves do? Like I have an infinite wellspring of love for whoever rewrote the gift list from the original Forsaken because Uratha used to be able to do everything from running faster to excreting fresh ground Columbian dark roast from their skin. You pull that last one out during game and suddenly all pretense that were are playing &quot;werewolves the tabletop&quot; is shattered. That's exactly the feeling I'm getting from being able to turn people wolf-blooded on sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because such a massive concentration of fear, desperation and trauma - hungry spirits wouldn't become an issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Uratha are predators: Morally sound actions are predicated by their necessity or lack of thereof, even as heinous as the scenario you just described, and that resembles some terrorist indoctrination and brain-washing tactic. Predators don't need to extend their prey's suffering beyond what is strictly necessary. The sheer idea of trying to &quot;take Luna's matters into your own hands&quot; would be likely more than disgusting for the five choirs of the Moon. I could see it being an effective tactic that the Pure enforce, but the problem with it was outlined by Charlaquin very aptly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Uratha don't know that a dramatic failure on a lunacy roll can make a human into a wolf-blooded. They don't even know what a dramatic failure or a lunacy roll is. All they know is that sometimes people who come into contact with werewolves become wolf-blooded, and sometimes they don't. It makes a lot of sense that myths would arise to try to explain a common factor among spontaneous adoptions, like &quot;it only happens if the werewolf bites you&quot; or &quot;it only happens on the full moon&quot; or what have you. The truth is Luna is not so consistent as that. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-14-2015, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T18:03:09-07:00","id":665107,"title":"","content":"DataWeaver: Really interesting points you are bringing up, actually. I think in the original Forsaken there was an explicit statement to the effect that all werewolves come from wolf-bloods and that being wolf-blooded was always genetic, but that was before tells when being wolf-blooded was nearly impossible to detect. Now there are ways to determine who is at risk of going full lychanthrope which has big implications for the setting vis-a-vis hunters. Also, big agreement noise from me about the abusive family dynamics in original Forsaken. Like the books literally assume that werewolf repopulation involves anonymous one-night stands with ignorant humans promptly followed by abandoned children because &quot;werwolves are too angry to raise families.&quot; Always hated that.<br /> <br /> Nofather: It says that the circumstances can't be machinated but then provides a way that they <i>can</i>. One of those statements must be false. So either a botched lunacy check does <i>not</i> always make a person wolf-blooded or it <i>does</i> in which case there's totally a reliable way to fabricate them. I edited my post after your reply I think, but with dominate gifts you could potentially turn those wolf-bloods to your cause or, more likely, recruit willing volunteers who want to join the gang that provides super powers as a fringe benefit. The Oath of the Moon wouldn't care for that of course, but werewolves don't generally police themselves as stringently as the Kindred do.<br /> <br /> What I <i>still</i> don't get is how becoming a wolf-blood through a botched lunacy check can be &quot;capricious Luna&quot; if it <i>always</i> happens. If botching a Lunacy check <i>always</i> makes a Wolf-Blood and that's a <i>rule</i> then I think that rule should be explained because it doesn't make a lot of sense by itself. Botching a Moon Taint roll could make you a wolf-blood and I'd totally accept that without further explanation, but why would just seeing a werewolf make you one??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T18:25:10-07:00","id":665115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665107#post665107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nofather: It says that the circumstances can't be machinated but then provides a way that they <i>can</i>. One of those statements must be false. So either a botched lunacy check does <i>not</i> always make a person wolf-blooded or it <i>does</i> in which case there's totally a reliable way to fabricate them. I edited my post after your reply I think, but with dominate gifts you could potentially turn those wolf-bloods to your cause or, more likely, recruit willing volunteers who want to join the gang that provides super powers as a fringe benefit. The Oath of the Moon wouldn't care for that of course, but werewolves don't generally police themselves as stringently as the Kindred do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Domination Gifts wouldn't really let you do that. You could force some social doors or lure a wolf-blooded into doing something but you wouldn't be able to make them a servant, and considering you just tortured them and drove them mad, as everyone pointed out, they're not likely to ever follow your cause unless you're going to force the torture a lot longer, which is a Pure tactic.<br /> <br /> As for whether werewolves police themselves, if you decide they don't in your game that's fine but the book suggests they are pretty severe about punishing wolves for breaking Oaths of the Moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I <i>still</i> don't get is how becoming a wolf-blood through a botched lunacy check can be &quot;capricious Luna&quot; if it <i>always</i> happens. If botching a Lunacy check <i>always</i> makes a Wolf-Blood and that's a <i>rule</i> then I think that rule should be explained because it doesn't make a lot of sense by itself. Botching a Moon Taint roll could make you a wolf-blood and I'd totally accept that without further explanation, but why would just seeing a werewolf make you one?? </div> </div> </div>The moon always goes around the Earth. The tides always come back in. She's not completely erratic. It's change, not random chaos. As for the inability to be machinated I figure she just disallows it if it's forced. It's her decision to make, not those of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-14-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:23:56-07:00","id":665294,"title":"","content":"A botched roll is an entirely meta-game concept. In character, it's entirely not definite when Lunacy does cause people to become Wolf-Blooded and when it doesent. The closest thing to a common factor might be that weak-willed people are adopted more often than strong-willed people (since it's a Resolve + Composure roll and you have to dramatically fail). But there's no in-character explanation to be had, since a dramatic failure isn't a thing that exists in-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:41:26-07:00","id":665302,"title":"","content":"With regards to Uratha oversight, which has been mentioned a few times now as a potential balancing point, there are certainly good in-character reasons for a lawful-good Uratha to not try and abuse this system. However I think the point about Pure and Bale Hounds is something to consider. No one tells the Predator Kings what to do, for example, and it would be perfectly appropriate for Rabid Wolf's children to abuse the mentally ill in order to &quot;spread their message.&quot; Those ideas right there are actually pretty good story hooks I think, so maybe consider that a vote in the rule's favor??<br /> <br /> Again though I stress that as written this rule about botched Lunacy checks is <i>not</i> a sometimes problem. As written it happens <i>every single time</i> a character botches that roll. That doesn't sound very &quot;random&quot; to me, or &quot;impossible to machinate.&quot; Why is this one of the few rules that Luna abides?<br /> <br /> Worth noting also is that it's not listed under the rules for Adoptions. We are <i>assuming</i> that the two are connected only because no other justification for the Lunacy botch rule was given, but they might be completely different rules. Luna might sometimes make humans Uratha or wolf-bloods on a whim and <i>that</i> might be impossible to machinate, but what if the Lunacy break rule is something else? Something which the writers completely failed to justify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:46:14-07:00","id":665304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665302#post665302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written it happens <i>every single time</i> a character botches that roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your persistent use of the term &quot;botch&quot; suggests to me that you are operating under a mistaken idea of how Dramatic Failures happen.<br /> <br /> You need a dicepool of <i>zero</i> to have it happen non-electively as a PC. The average mortal character has a base Resolve + Composure pool of four or five dice and you need to be in Gauru to take any dice off of that before Primal Urge <i>4.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-14-2015, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:57:07-07:00","id":665338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665302#post665302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Uratha oversight, which has been mentioned a few times now as a potential balancing point, there are certainly good in-character reasons for a lawful-good Uratha to not try and abuse this system. However I think the point about Pure and Bale Hounds is something to consider. No one tells the Predator Kings what to do, for example, and it would be perfectly appropriate for Rabid Wolf's children to abuse the mentally ill in order to &quot;spread their message.&quot; Those ideas right there are actually pretty good story hooks I think, so maybe consider that a vote in the rule's favor??</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't believe werewolves police their own, there's a section after the Oath of the Moon detailing Oathbreakers and what happens to them, and an entire tribe focused on hunting down other werewolves. You don't have to be 'lawful good' to not try to drive people into madness so that they might kill you. For the other factions, it ignores the pretentiousness of the Pure. The Pure believe they are special, they honor the hunt, the spirit, and their families, respectively. Bringing non-hunters and people with no sense of the spirit or, worse, people not related to them would probably be abhorrent to them. And the Bale Hounds don't have any reason to make new werewolves, they corrupt humans and werewolves alike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again though I stress that as written this rule about botched Lunacy checks is <i>not</i> a sometimes problem. As written it happens <i>every single time</i> a character botches that roll. That doesn't sound very &quot;random&quot; to me, or &quot;impossible to machinate.&quot; Why is this one of the few rules that Luna abides?<br /> <br /> Worth noting also is that it's not listed under the rules for Adoptions. We are <i>assuming</i> that the two are connected only because no other justification for the Lunacy botch rule was given, but they might be completely different rules. Luna might sometimes make humans Uratha or wolf-bloods on a whim and <i>that</i> might be impossible to machinate, but what if the Lunacy break rule is something else? Something which the writers completely failed to justify? </div> </div> </div>Luna abides many rules. Silver, the brands of renown, the Oaths of the Moon. As I said, she's not a god of randomness. As for the writers failing to justify things there are other books on the horizon that may make things more clear for you, but the book as it is is pretty clear. A dramatic failure, which isn't an in-world concept, and is rare, as Satchel pointed out you need a dice pool of 0 <i>and </i>to roll a 1 on your chance roll, can turn people into wolf-blooded, except when machinated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2015, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T22:09:08-07:00","id":665388,"title":"","content":"Page 159 of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd ed: &quot;Dramatic failure: ... Suffered when you roll a 1 on a chance die. Alternatively, you can take a Beat in exchange for turning a normal failure into a dramatic failure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 101 of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd ed, under Lunacy rules: &quot;On a dramatic failure, she becomes Wolf-Blooded,&quot;<br /> <br /> These are the two relevant facts from the rule book we have available. My original question which I consider unanswered as of yet was &quot;why does dramatically failing a Lunacy roll make you a wolf-blood?&quot;<br /> <br /> It was then suggested that this was due to Luna &quot;randomly&quot; selecting people to make wolf-blooded as per the rules for Adoption on page 296. However, the rules for adoption specifically state that there is no rhyme or reason for this. It happens when and if Luna feels so inclined. This is <i>not the case</i> for Lunacy rules, which state quite clearly that <i>any</i> time you dramatically fail a lunacy check you <i>always</i> become wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> As these two things are categorically incompatible with each other, then one of the two rules is false. If not, then there must be a separate reason why dramatically failing a lunacy check results in wolf-bloods because this system <i>does not</i> meet the requirements for Adoption, i.e. that they must be completely random and non-repeatable. What is the flaw with my logic here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T22:13:17-07:00","id":665391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665302#post665302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again though I stress that as written this rule about botched Lunacy checks is <i>not</i> a sometimes problem. As written it happens <i>every single time</i> a character botches that roll. That doesn't sound very &quot;random&quot; to me, or &quot;impossible to machinate.&quot; Why is this one of the few rules that Luna abides?</div> </div> </div> </div>It happens every single time the character rolls a 1 on their chance die, yeah. (10% of the time, it works every time!) Of course, in order to be rolling a chance die in the first place, you need to have a dice pool of 0, which as Satchel pointed out is actually very difficult to do. Of course, if it's a PC making the roll and they fail, they can opt to take a Dramatic Failure for the Beat, but that's a special case. Of course, Uratha have no concept of dice rolls, chance dice, dramatic failures, or Beats. From an in-character perspective, what it <i>looks like</i> is that the vast majority of the time, people who experience Lunacy don't become Wolf-Blooded. But sometimes, very rarely and with no discernible reason (because there's no way a character in-game would be able to discern that the victim rolled a dramatic failure, since dramatic failures don't exist as an in-universe concept), they do become Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2015, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T22:19:30-07:00","id":665393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665388#post665388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As these two things are categorically incompatible with each other, then one of the two rules is false. If not, then there must be a separate reason why dramatically failing a lunacy check results in wolf-bloods because this system <i>does not</i> meet the requirements for Adoption, i.e. that they must be completely random and non-repeatable. What is the flaw with my logic here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The flaw with your logic here is that a chance roll is not going to happen on all or even most Lunacy checks by the simple facts of how the penalties work and that NPCs do not get the option of upgrading on account of how they don't track or use Beats.<br /> <br /> The most likely causes after accounting for the societal taboo against revealing your nature to humans are that you have missed a lone witness and are using the killing form and/or happen to be a significantly potent avatar of the Hunt \u2014 anyone with even a remotely above-average Resolve + Composure total is going to take a Gauru-form werewolf of Primal Urge <i>8 or more</i> to run the risk of &quot;infection.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a decent amount of folkloric material about the Wild Hunt to work with here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T22:53:29-07:00","id":665407,"title":"","content":"Are you assuming that NPCs cannot opt into a dramatic failure the way a PC can in order to take a beat? If so, I begin to see your logic. One does not &quot;always&quot; become wolf-blooded from failing a Lunacy check, that much is true. It would <i>seem</i> pretty random from the outside since only 10% of a slim minority would turn wolf-blooded. In my own games I assume that NPCs are &quot;actors&quot; and thus can suffer voluntary handicaps that grant PCs experience not for mechanical benefits but because it suits their &quot;role.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your own rules are just as legitimate, but these results would still be repeatable: you'd just have to lower a person's Resolve + Composure pool before exposing them to Lunacy. If that meant that inflicting Lunacy on the mentally ill often resulted in wolf-bloods, then that at least would seem thematic. More likely though I return to the prison-camp thought experiment: repeatedly exposing people to a werewolf in <i>dalu </i>until their minds broke and they were suddenly part of the family.<br /> <br /> But the question is not &quot;is that a good idea&quot; but rather &quot;does it make sense for that to be possible.&quot; I would say no for the same reason I objected to werewolves being able to shoot lasers out their eyes in the previous edition: it's simply not something werewolves <i>do</i>. If you say that <i>your </i>werewolves <i>can</i> shoot lasers from their eyes in your stories that's fine, except if I play <i>your</i> werewolf game I'm no longer playing the same monsters I loved in <i>Wolfman</i>, <i>Ginger Snaps</i>, <i>Wolf</i> and the <i>Howling</i>. Preserving that experience is important, and I personally feel like this rule gets in the way of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T23:03:46-07:00","id":665410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665407#post665407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More likely though I return to the prison-camp thought experiment: repeatedly exposing people to a werewolf in <i>dalu </i>until their minds broke and they were suddenly part of the family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dalu is literally <i>the least useful form for this purpose.</i><br /> <br /> Gauru is the only form that incurs a penalty to the Lunacy check, its controlled use is strictly budgeted, and the best means of circumventing that timer without losing your mind explicitly downgrades the form's impact on the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-15-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T23:19:19-07:00","id":665418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665410#post665410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dalu is literally <i>the least useful form for this purpose.</i><br /> <br /> Gauru is the only form that incurs a penalty to the Lunacy check, its controlled use is strictly budgeted, and the best means of circumventing that timer without losing your mind explicitly downgrades the form's impact on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, however, impose multiple penalties on a person's Resolve + Composure by making them sleep deprived, hungry, agitated and drugged, possibly from more than one substance, such that their roll was at negatives <i>before</i> the bonus for Dalu or Urshual form was applied, keeping them at zero or below for that roll.<br /> <br /> Again though, this issue is an academic one. The fact remains that it is <i>possible</i> to force a person to become wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. It's possible, demonstrable and it's repeatable. This rule's existence means that you can &quot;catch lychanthropy&quot; just from<i> seeing</i> a Dalu werewolf in its boxer shorts, and I still see no reason why that should be included in the lore of werewolves here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T23:29:24-07:00","id":665421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665418#post665418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could, however, impose multiple penalties on a person's Resolve + Composure by making them sleep deprived, hungry, agitated and drugged, possibly from more than one substance, such that their roll was at negatives <i>before</i> the bonus for Dalu or Urshual form was applied, keeping them at zero or below for that roll.<br /> <br /> Again though, this issue is an academic one. The fact remains that it is <i>possible</i> to force a person to become wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. It's possible, demonstrable and it's repeatable. This rule's existence means that you can &quot;catch lychanthropy&quot; just from<i> seeing</i> a Dalu werewolf in its boxer shorts, and I still see no reason why that should be included in the lore of werewolves here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to be suggesting that the existence of a bizarre and contrived edge case defeats the function of the mechanic, which is that isolated and unstable people who witness the depredations of a powerful werewolf are likely to awaken their latent shapeshifter heritage if they don't instead lose yet more of their self-concept and go mad, go berserk, or become an even tastier snack than usual for werewolves.<br /> <br /> You also appear to be suggesting that every wolf-blood becomes a werewolf and/or that every Tell is discernible as &quot;lycanthropy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:00:20-07:00","id":665423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665418#post665418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could, however, impose multiple penalties on a person's Resolve + Composure by making them sleep deprived, hungry, agitated and drugged, possibly from more than one substance, such that their roll was at negatives <i>before</i> the bonus for Dalu or Urshual form was applied, keeping them at zero or below for that roll.<br /> <br /> Again though, this issue is an academic one. The fact remains that it is <i>possible</i> to force a person to become wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. It's possible, demonstrable and it's repeatable. This rule's existence means that you can &quot;catch lychanthropy&quot; just from<i> seeing</i> a Dalu werewolf in its boxer shorts, and I still see no reason why that should be included in the lore of werewolves here.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, again, in character, no one <i>knows</i> that you can become a wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. Lunacy turning people Wolf-Blooded is supposed to be the source of myths like &quot;if a werewolf bites you, you become one&quot;. They're just that though, myths. The truth is that what turns you Wolf-Blooded is being in the presence of the sheer unbridled power of wolf and moon embodied in the werewolf, and being so completely unable to handle that experience that it changes you on a metaphysical level. The fact that he also bit you is actually incidental, but you don't know that. And neither does the werewolf. This gives Forsaken its own unique take on werewolf lore, whilst also providing an in-universe explanation of where the traditional myths and legends came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:09:30-07:00","id":665428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665421#post665421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You appear to be suggesting that the existence of a bizarre and contrived edge case defeats the function of the mechanic, which is that isolated and unstable people who witness the depredations of a powerful werewolf are likely to awaken their latent shapeshifter heritage if they don't instead lose yet more of their self-concept and go mad, go berserk, or become an even tastier snack than usual for werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I'm saying I haven't heard a reason why the mechanic exists <i>in the first place</i>. If I'm understanding you correctly though your take is that every human being is at least a little wolf-blooded and seeing a werewolf in action &quot;inspires&quot; you to be more so? Is that what your canon is? I don't see a lot of justification for that in the book but it's a theory at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665421#post665421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also appear to be suggesting that every wolf-blood becomes a werewolf and/or that every Tell is discernible as &quot;lycanthropy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Catch lychanthropy&quot; was in ironic quotes because I got sick of writing &quot;turn into a wolf-blood who might also turn into an <i>uratha</i> but also might just turn directly into an <i>uratha </i>and skip that step.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665423#post665423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, again, in character, no one <i>knows</i> that you can become a wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. Lunacy turning people Wolf-Blooded is supposed to be the source of myths like &quot;if a werewolf bites you, you become one&quot;. They're just that though, myths. The truth is that what turns you Wolf-Blooded is being in the presence of the sheer unbridled power of wolf and moon embodied in the werewolf, and being so completely unable to handle that experience that it changes you on a metaphysical level. The fact that he also bit you is actually incidental, but you don't know that. And neither does the werewolf. This gives Forsaken its own unique take on werewolf lore, whilst also providing an in-universe explanation of where the traditional myths and legends came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so again seems like you subscribe to an &quot;inspiration&quot; interpretation where just seeing a werewolf can give you some wolf powers. Are all humans &quot;potential werewolves&quot; then? We just need to believe that they exist and that's a passage to becoming one?<br /> <br /> I mean that's fine, if so. I can't think of anything that super breaks if that's true. It's just as valid as <i>not</i> including the rule, which is what I still plan to do. Frankly I think it's pretty equivalent to substituting a &quot;surviving a werewolf attack makes you a werewolf&quot; rule and a good sight less supported by the lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:33:10-07:00","id":665436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665428#post665428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I'm saying I haven't heard a reason why the mechanic exists <i>in the first place</i>. If I'm understanding you correctly though your take is that every human being is at least a little wolf-blooded and seeing a werewolf in action &quot;inspires&quot; you to be more so? Is that what your canon is? I don't see a lot of justification for that in the book but it's a theory at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as I have &quot;a canon&quot; for the purposes of discussion, it's the content of the books that I've read for the World of Darkness as a whole. Latent supernatural powers are not a thing that is unique to any gameline and the particulars of &quot;bloodline&quot; get weird when spiritual &quot;parentage&quot; is frequently adoptive and werewolves regularly have kids who don't grow up to be werewolves or wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Catch lychanthropy&quot; was in ironic quotes because I got sick of writing &quot;turn into a wolf-blood who might also turn into an <i>uratha</i> but also might just turn directly into an <i>uratha </i>and skip that step.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And your admission of this only serves to further weaken your argument that there's a problem, because you're getting into vanishingly smaller chances if you don't actively stack a scenario against it.<br /> <br /> If you keep finding yourself exposed to Lunacy under conditions that allow for dramatic failure, the post-hoc narrative that's likely to be applied is that the fickle goddess of fate that is Mother Luna saw fit to expose you to stimuli that led to you opening your eyes to Her children's world. It's similar to how revenants rise in Vampire or Family Ties are formed in Beast \u2014 there's mechanics, yes, but broadly speaking they're random rolls that serve to emphasize the uncertainty of the related phenomena from a humanlike perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:42:00-07:00","id":665442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665436#post665436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your admission of this only serves to further weaken your argument that there's a problem, because you're getting into vanishingly smaller chances if you don't actively stack a scenario against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an argument that I'm making? I'm literally asking a question? &quot;Why does failing a lunacy check make you wolf-blooded&quot; is not answered by saying &quot;it probably won't happen, don't worry about it&quot; which appears to be what you're saying to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665436#post665436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you keep finding yourself exposed to Lunacy under conditions that allow for dramatic failure, the post-hoc narrative that's likely to be applied is that the fickle goddess of fate that is Mother Luna saw fit to expose you to stimuli that led to you opening your eyes to Her children's world. It's similar to how revenants rise in Vampire or Family Ties are formed in Beast \u2014 there's mechanics, yes, but broadly speaking they're random rolls that serve to emphasize the uncertainty of the related phenomena from a humanlike perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Luna just randomly makes people wolf-bloods or even actual <i>uratha</i> that's fine, but we don't need concrete rules for that, then. Saying &quot;this just happens sometimes for no reason&quot; followed immediately by &quot;here's a situation when it <i>always</i> happens&quot; is contradictory, and that is <i>exactly</i> what is happening with these rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:47:47-07:00","id":665445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665442#post665442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Luna just randomly makes people wolf-bloods or even actual <i>uratha</i> that's fine, but we don't need concrete rules for that, then. Saying &quot;this just happens sometimes for no reason&quot; followed immediately by &quot;here's a situation when it <i>always</i> happens&quot; is contradictory, and that is <i>exactly</i> what is happening with these rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've demonstrated an extremely nonstandard definition of the word &quot;always,&quot; which is why your larger question of &quot;why does this happen at all?&quot; is falling by the wayside in the answering.<br /> <br /> &quot;At some point after a random length of time in the next twenty-eight days of witnessing something that werewolves culturally permit <i>murder </i>for, you undergo a breakdown and develop magical powers and/or qualities if you were lucky enough to be present and unaccounted for at the scene of a powerful werewolf acting at their most visibly lycanthropic.&quot; This is, to most casual inspection, indistinguishable from &quot;This just happens sometimes for no reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:03:01-07:00","id":665468,"title":"","content":"Failing the check <i>doesn't</i> make you wolf blooded. It is simply a way of randomising an insane deities fickle whims. The storyteller can just go &quot;well, they rolled a one, but I don't feel like bringing them back so I'll just ignore it&quot; or &quot;that was a regular fail but sod it, I'll make them wolf blooded anyway&quot; if they want, and a player taking a beat is momentarily playing Luna when they do. <br /> <br /> Lunacy is a momentary connection to a werewolf's spiritual nature. One that Luna can use to give you a shove into her purview if she chooses. The only random part is whether or not she did. And why does this happen? Because at some point Luna, a rank 8/9 godlike being, decided it did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:09:28-07:00","id":665470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665445#post665445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've demonstrated an extremely nonstandard definition of the word &quot;always,&quot; which is why your larger question of &quot;why does this happen at all?&quot; is falling by the wayside in the answering.<br /> <br /> &quot;At some point after a random length of time in the next twenty-eight days of witnessing something that werewolves culturally permit <i>murder </i>for, you undergo a breakdown and develop magical powers and/or qualities if you were lucky enough to be present and unaccounted for at the scene of a powerful werewolf acting at their most visibly lycanthropic.&quot; This is, to most casual inspection, indistinguishable from &quot;This just happens sometimes for no reason.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are assuming that the same rules that apply to adoption apply to the failed lunacy rules. Again, I think these are actually different sets of rules. Even if it weren't though, the rules for adoption say that the victim will experience strange happenings and expanded senses prior to &quot;officially&quot; becoming wolf blooded on the next moon of the appropriate type. So it would actually be pretty easy to form the connection. Also, if someone not of the blood becomes wolf blooded you look at what contact they've had with the people and determine that literally <i>all</i> they did was see someone in dalu form last week. Like it's &quot;the same thing&quot; to a casual observer if the casual observer is really really clueless I guess, but otherwise I think a connection would be pretty damned easy to spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:36:50-07:00","id":665485,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they are different. The Lunacy rules provide a randomised way of letting the dice decide, whereas adoption is just &quot;whenever the storyteller feels like it&quot;. Or justifications for a mortal player to buy the Tell merit. <br /> <br /> In-universe though, it's all the same shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:36:57-07:00","id":665486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665423#post665423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, again, in character, no one <i>knows</i> that you can become a wolf-blooded just from seeing a werewolf. Lunacy turning people Wolf-Blooded is supposed to be the source of myths like &quot;if a werewolf bites you, you become one&quot;. They're just that though, myths. The truth is that what turns you Wolf-Blooded is being in the presence of the sheer unbridled power of wolf and moon embodied in the werewolf, and being so completely unable to handle that experience that it changes you on a metaphysical level. The fact that he also bit you is actually incidental, but you don't know that. And neither does the werewolf. This gives Forsaken its own unique take on werewolf lore, whilst also providing an in-universe explanation of where the traditional myths and legends came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add, doesn't people even take a bonus to lunacy rolls upon being damaged by a werewolf in such a hybrid form, on account of the sheer lucidity of the experience? (I honestly don't recall if it was a penalty or a bonus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:39:14-07:00","id":665488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665428#post665428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I'm saying I haven't heard a reason why the mechanic exists <i>in the first place</i>. If I'm understanding you correctly though your take is that every human being is at least a little wolf-blooded and seeing a werewolf in action &quot;inspires&quot; you to be more so? Is that what your canon is? I don't see a lot of justification for that in the book but it's a theory at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the mechanic is to display more lycanthropic myths in the setting. One of them being that lycanthropy is indeed, a disease (infectious or sexually transmitted) of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:41:48-07:00","id":665490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665468#post665468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Failing the check <i>doesn't</i> make you wolf blooded. It is simply a way of randomising an insane deities fickle whims. The storyteller can just go &quot;well, they rolled a one, but I don't feel like bringing them back so I'll just ignore it&quot; or &quot;that was a regular fail but sod it, I'll make them wolf blooded anyway&quot; if they want, and a player taking a beat is momentarily playing Luna when they do.<br /> <br /> Lunacy is a momentary connection to a werewolf's spiritual nature. One that Luna can use to give you a shove into her purview if she chooses. The only random part is whether or not she did. And why does this happen? Because at some point Luna, a rank 8/9 godlike being, decided it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this illustrates why STs should always have Screens and roll their dice behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:46:35-07:00","id":665492,"title":"","content":"Yeah. &quot;I got bit by a wolf monster and then next full moon I turned into one&quot; is a thing that has almost certainly happened, thanks to the Shape-Shifted tell. And, y'know, by most real-world definitions they <i>are</i> a werewolf at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T08:41:52-07:00","id":665793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665470#post665470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like it's &quot;the same thing&quot; to a casual observer if the casual observer is really really clueless I guess, but otherwise I think a connection would be pretty damned easy to spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are five or six days in the twenty-eight days of a lunar month that a new wolf-blood is marginally more likely to come into their abilities on out of an otherwise random selection. Which five or six days those are depends on the auspice of the werewolf that activated them, when the vast majority of humanity is not even aware that moon-auspices are a thing that werewolves have. The six-day periods are split into two three-day clumps, and one of the five-day periods is associated with the auspice built for stealth and cunning, which leaves the most visible instances of mortal witnesses becoming wolf-blooded as people who make the change in the half-week or less immediately following the killing blow of a moderately powerful Rahu.<br /> <br /> Witnesses of a werewolf attack that werewolves know about tend to be followed up on due to culturally and spiritually weighted paranoia, and witnesses who are not presently wolf-blooded but clearly remember the event are generally considered fair game for summary murder (it's even something you can earn Renown for); most Lunacy-induced wolf-blooded are therefore going to be witnesses the werewolves didn't know about.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded Tells further manifest in a wide variety of fashions which may not always be clearly delineated in when they finish coming in, and not having the memory banished from your mind doesn't give the character a flawless understanding of what's happened or fix the exact dates of both events in their mind, much less prompt them to volunteer that information when they find their way into a wolf-cult.<br /> <br /> A &quot;casual observer&quot; in all this is not<i> omniscient</i>, nor are they clueless for not putting together information that includes several random lengths of time, supernatural oversights, and points of mental fatigue to get anything more concrete than &quot;spontaneous wolf-blooded might be more common in areas where powerful werewolves hunt frequently and carelessly in the world of flesh in defiance of their nature and society,&quot; which it's not hard for the urban-legend rumor-mill to attribute to divine retribution from the Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-15-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:38:40-07:00","id":665939,"title":"","content":"Elfive: I think your comment about Lunacy being a direct link to Luna was an edit I missed? That's actually a pretty reasonable reason for this rule, I wish I'd seen it earlier. Again, I don't think that's explicitly stated, but since the Hisil is a &quot;conceptual space&quot; as much as a physical one it makes sense to me that certain thought patterns or emotions place mortals closer to the incarnae, with Lunacy being very close real estate to Luna herself. Pretty ace reasoning honestly, though I still prefer the classic &quot;bite makes you a werewolf&quot; mechanics and will probably use those instead.<br /> <br /> Satchel: You're adding way more complexity than I think functionally exists. Obviously if a casual observer never <i>notices</i> the wolf-blood after their turning then they won't have any ability to guess how they came to be. But anyone who does take notice, like a pack of werewolves patrolling their territory responsibly, could question the new wolf-blood and figure it out by process of elimination. Average Joe wasn't any kind of supernatural until that night he saw the pack omega buying cigarettes in dalu form, and a couple days or weeks later he was seeing the ghost of the radio age in his favorite Starbucks. <i>Not</i> a difficult connection to make if you are trying to establish a root cause, which at least some uratha would want to do in order to uphold the secrecy of their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:42:54-07:00","id":665988,"title":"","content":"If you want to know the real reason the rule exists, I'm sure it went something like this: The developers were sitting around a table brainstorming when one of them comes up with the idea of unintended consequences. You go garu in a crowd and some of the survivors in that crowd become wolf blooded (ie, interesting npcs) who then come looking for you in a way that might or might not be good for you but surely makes the story more interesting. This was then followed by someone suggesting that having an origin story were the once mortal character witnesses a werewolf and then finds his world turned upside down until he to changes sounds a lot more interesting and dramatic than puberty came and gave me zits, hair and fangs. Followed by the collective group saying &quot;yea, that's cool&quot; and thus a rule was born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T17:37:26-07:00","id":666227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665939#post665939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive: I think your comment about Lunacy being a direct link to Luna was an edit I missed? That's actually a pretty reasonable reason for this rule, I wish I'd seen it earlier. Again, I don't think that's explicitly stated, but since the Hisil is a &quot;conceptual space&quot; as much as a physical one it makes sense to me that certain thought patterns or emotions place mortals closer to the incarnae, with Lunacy being very close real estate to Luna herself. Pretty ace reasoning honestly, though I still prefer the classic &quot;bite makes you a werewolf&quot; mechanics and will probably use those instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, the mind breaking visage of an Uratha in his hybrid forms was explicitly stated to be of Luna's providence in the previous edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665939#post665939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel: You're adding way more complexity than I think functionally exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odd, what you call 'complexity' I call taking all the variables into account that do in fact put a wedge in your idea's concept, to their most sensible values. See why a 'casual observer' can't be omniscient.<br /> <br /> Unless said casual observer is basically Sherlock Holmes. With a degree in Shadow Resonance and metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-15-2015, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T18:46:56-07:00","id":666293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665939#post665939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel: You're adding way more complexity than I think functionally exists. Obviously if a casual observer never <i>notices</i> the wolf-blood after their turning then they won't have any ability to guess how they came to be. But anyone who does take notice, like a pack of werewolves patrolling their territory responsibly, could question the new wolf-blood and figure it out by process of elimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves that are patrolling their territory responsibly would most likely kill him before he even had a chance to manifest a Tell. People who witness werewolves in the hybrid forms and remember it are a threat to the security of the Oath, and should be dealt with as quickly as possible. If by chance the pack wasn't aware that this human witnessed them, the only way they're even going to know he saw them is if he tells them so. Even then, there's no actual evidence indicating that seeing the werewolves was the reason he gained a Tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=665939#post665939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average Joe wasn't any kind of supernatural until that night he saw the pack omega buying cigarettes in dalu form, and a couple days or weeks later he was seeing the ghost of the radio age in his favorite Starbucks. <i>Not</i> a difficult connection to make if you are trying to establish a root cause, which at least some uratha would want to do in order to uphold the secrecy of their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a huge logical leap. Correlation does not imply causation, and the fact that this guy saw the dalu buying cigarettes a few weeks before he gained his Tell does not imply that it's the reason he gained the Tell. To assume otherwise is just bad science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T23:49:57-07:00","id":666531,"title":"","content":"&quot;I saw a really big hairy dude one time and now I see dead people.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, totally obvious. How could you not see the connection there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:16:27-07:00","id":666545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=666531#post666531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I saw a really big hairy dude one time and now I see dead people.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, totally obvious. How could you not see the connection there?</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of Dalu in the example makes the connection even stronger, because there's an unrepeated &quot;while I was <i>zonked out of my fucking skull</i>&quot; required to make it work at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T01:06:29-07:00","id":666609,"title":"","content":"It also works if the guy had shitty resolve and composure, and the omega was primal urge 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:47:58-07:00","id":667066,"title":"","content":"I'd hate to see the alpha of that pack.<br /> <br /> But don't forget after that the human's had ten days of Atavism, where they're attacking everything dangerous or stressful especially the source of their Lunacy, Delusion where they're fleeing from the supernatural and risking catatonia if they can't, or Reception where they become an Essence generator for nearby spirits and, with their horrible Attributes, can just fall into the Hisil upon suffering a dramatic failure. Where presumably they would never be heard from again. And your memories are still mixed up along with the issues of a regular failure, as confirmed by one of the developers, destroying my arguments to suggest otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:28:13-07:00","id":667286,"title":"","content":"Yes, Dramatic Failure on Lunacy still smacks you with the regular failure effects as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:13:46-07:00","id":676157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=666293#post666293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a huge logical leap. Correlation does not imply causation, and the fact that this guy saw the dalu buying cigarettes a few weeks before he gained his Tell does not imply that it's the reason he gained the Tell. To assume otherwise is just bad science.</div> </div> </div> </div>It *is* but it's also how virtually all science happens. You observe phenomena and you develop what you believe to be the best theory for how it came to be, then you test it. You aren't <i>supposed</i> to develop those theories going in but everyone does, that's called inductive reasoning and we do it because it seems to save time when we have working models that explain most of an otherwise unexplained event.<br /> <br /> Here's the logical breakdown I see for someone who has discovered a newly turned uratha or wolfblood: They are this thing <i>now</i>, but they weren't this thing <i>before</i>, so that means that something has changed. This must have happened prior to their first change.<br /> &quot;Has anything weird happened to you lately mr werewolf sir?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well <i>yes</i> doctor, now that you mention it my life has been a veritable circus of paranormal activity ever since a certain night three weeks ago when I saw a man who was clearly a werewolf beneath the light of the full moon.&quot;<br /> &quot;Interesting,&quot; says the doctor, &quot;but let's not jump to any conclusions. Was there any <i>other</i> event prior to this that might have resulted in you turning into a crazy wolf man?&quot;<br /> &quot;No,&quot; says the presumably bound patient, &quot;not unless my nan was right and this is some ad absurdum instance of hairy palms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like maybe this paritcular uratha was also abducted by aliens at some point prior, that would mix the result sup, but <i>probably not</i>. Like most people int he world of darkness he was probably living an ordinary life uninformed about supernatural entities until he suddenly became one. I don't think it's <i>any</i> kind of stretch to say that people would find a correlation between seeing werewolves and becoming them if such a correlation existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:20:44-07:00","id":676161,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, this logic falls flat when you recall that Lunacy also blurs memories of the event that caused it, so anyone who becomes wolf blooded due to seeing a werewolf isn't going to <i>remember</i> seeing a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:23:49-07:00","id":676163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676161#post676161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, this logic falls flat when you recall that Lunacy also blurs memories of the event that caused it, so anyone who becomes wolf blooded due to seeing a werewolf isn't going to <i>remember</i> seeing a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent point. They would probably remember a &quot;crazy night&quot; and the date of that night but not the specifics of what had happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:03:17-07:00","id":676313,"title":"","content":"More likely they would remember the specifics, but those specifics would be altered to make things not a 'crazy night.' You wouldn't see a werewolf beneath the full moon, for instance, but a bear or large man beneath the full moon. Which may be common enough that it might be forgotten or blend in with other memories of seeing people.<br /> <br /> And one doesn't instantly become a wolf-blooded or suffer the effects of Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:43:35-07:00","id":676628,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's not &quot;I've been seeing spirits ever since this night last month when I saw a werewolf.&quot; It's &quot;I've been seeing spirits ever since this night three weeks ago, for no apparent reason&quot;, and that night happened to have been 10 days after the night that you saw a big lumberjack-looking dude buying cigarettes at a gas station, which would not seem like an unusual or even very noteworthy event, especially since it happened several days before any of the supernatural weirdness started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-24-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:39:33-07:00","id":676725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676313#post676313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one doesn't instantly become a wolf-blooded or suffer the effects of Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that because of the rules for Adoption though? Because again I think these might be different rule sets. It might be instantaneous int he case of a Lunacy dramatic failure. Though I guess in that case you'd suddenly be immune to lunacy which i guess is not the case so... I dunno?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:52:27-07:00","id":676731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676725#post676725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that because of the rules for Adoption though? Because again I think these might be different rule sets. It might be instantaneous int he case of a Lunacy dramatic failure. Though I guess in that case you'd suddenly be immune to lunacy which i guess is not the case so... I dunno?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's right under the rules for Lunacy.<br /> <br /> 'Sometimes, just sometimes, Wolf-Blooded arise from the taint of Lunacy, not from genetics. Any time a human suffers a dramatic failure on the Lunacy breaking point roll, she becomes Wolf-Blooded. This doesn\u2019t take instantly. It occurs at a seemingly random moon phase over the course of the next lunar month.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:59:20-07:00","id":676738,"title":"","content":"I don't know why you think they're different. One is a way you get wolf blooded from lunacy, while the other is a way you get wolf blooded from lunacy. <br /> <br /> The character's don't roll dice, y'know. There is no difference in-universe between the random number god and the random whim of the storyteller. Shit just happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T20:22:01-07:00","id":677197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676725#post676725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that because of the rules for Adoption though? Because again I think these might be different rule sets. It might be instantaneous int he case of a Lunacy dramatic failure. Though I guess in that case you'd suddenly be immune to lunacy which i guess is not the case so... I dunno?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunacy is the deep down, ancestral fear of the wolf at the door. When a person sees a werewolf in Dalu, Gauru, or Urshul up close, or witnesses a werewolf shapeshifting or regenerating damage, she suffers a breaking point. <b>The roll doesn\u2019t necessarily come immediately; it comes at the dramatically appropriate moment when the witness would otherwise take a rational breath and come to her senses.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T12:05:14-07:00","id":681295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=677197#post677197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please read the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's clearly talking about the Breaking Point roll, <i>not</i> the roll to resist Lunacy. Like really use your head. If you had to wait to roll Lunacy until <i>after</i> you'd seen a werewolf in Garu form you wouldn't know if you had failed the roll for an intense condition or succeeded and gotten a lesser version of it. And in the mean time is your character fine? Do they suffer the lesser condition by default, the greater or both?<br /> <br /> If you ever made a worthwhile comment then maybe I'd actually consider your feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 09-28-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T12:12:22-07:00","id":681302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676731#post676731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's right under the rules for Lunacy.<br /> <br /> 'Sometimes, just sometimes, Wolf-Blooded arise from the taint of Lunacy, not from genetics. Any time a human suffers a dramatic failure on the Lunacy breaking point roll, she becomes Wolf-Blooded. This doesn\u2019t take instantly. It occurs at a seemingly random moon phase over the course of the next lunar month.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right, forgot about that bit of text, good show.<br /> <br /> Elfive: With the way it's separated in the book into two different sections, one on random adoptions by Luna and one as a sub heading on Lunacy, PLUS the fact that Luna does canonically turn people who were never exposed to Lunacy in the Adoption section, I think it's very <i>possible</i> that these are different rules. Now it may be that all instances of a person becoming wolf-blooded from Lunacy exposure is a form of Adoption, but it's not true that every adoption involves Lunacy so I think at best these are rules under different headings with quite possibly different mechanics. If you want to treat them as Luna's personal interest then you could but I personally don't think that jives with the fact that there are actual solid and repeatable mechanics for the Lunacy turning. To me, these seem like different methods for arriving at the same conclusion.<br /> <br /> And again on the topic of NPCs not making rolls that's just not how I've ever played this game. Like those dice are there to represent mortals trying something which they may or may not succeed at, I think everyone gets those. If I don't roll for my NPCs then it's usually just because the roll was trivial or contested to such a degree that it wasn't worth the time, but those rolls still happen in my head. Again, I think your way is valid, but it's just not mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 09-28-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T12:30:11-07:00","id":681312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681295#post681295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's clearly talking about the Breaking Point roll, <i>not</i> the roll to resist Lunacy. Like really use your head. If you had to wait to roll Lunacy until <i>after</i> you'd seen a werewolf in Garu form you wouldn't know if you had failed the roll for an intense condition or succeeded and gotten a lesser version of it. And in the mean time is your character fine? Do they suffer the lesser condition by default, the greater or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Breaking Point roll is the roll for Lunacy, they are one in the same. Sometimes you do have to wait for Lunacy until after you've seen a werewolf. For instance if a bunch of hunters find someone suspicious while investigating a series of animal mutilations, they push him around a bit, he transforms, they can still fight. But when they're in the hospital later on, their memories may rearrange to something more acceptable and they may suffer the various Lunacy Conditions.<br /> <br /> It depends on the situation, but this is explicitly called out in the book as Satchel mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T13:30:08-07:00","id":681374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=676738#post676738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character's don't roll dice, y'know. There is no difference in-universe between the random number god and the random whim of the storyteller. Shit just happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681302#post681302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again on the topic of NPCs not making rolls that's just not how I've ever played this game. Like those dice are there to represent mortals trying something which they may or may not succeed at, I think everyone gets those. If I don't roll for my NPCs then it's usually just because the roll was trivial or contested to such a degree that it wasn't worth the time, but those rolls still happen in my head. Again, I think your way is valid, but it's just not mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elfive isn't talking about NPCs not getting to make the roll, he's talking about in-character knowledge versus out-of-character knowledge (I think. Elfive, please correct me if I'm wrong). If you want to let NPCs roll to resist Lunacy, feel free. That's perfectly within the bounds of the rules, the only reason I chose not to is because I find it to be one of those trivial rolls you mentioned. YMMV.<br /> <br /> What he means (again, unless I'm mistaken) is that, while you as the ST are rolling dice on behalf of the NPCs, the NPCs themselves are not rolling dice in-universe, and have no knowledge of the result of your roll.<br /> <br /> Out of character, the dice act as a random number generator to determine, at random, one of several possible outcomes. In-character, there are no dice, only the random whims of Luna. But both in and out of character, the result is determined in part by random chance. In other words, the dice act as a stand-in for Luna's whims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:31:24-07:00","id":681529,"title":"","content":"Nofather: But aren't some of the Lunacy conditions, particularly for failure, still things like running away screaming and fainting spells? That doesn't strike me as a very thematic thing to happen only LATER when you are in a safe place and no longer under the direct effects of Luna's touch. Frankly I think that Hunters encountering a werewolf in Garu form SHOULD suffer debilitating effects upon seeing them, unless they came prepared with some sort of Lunacy counter measures not described in the Forsaken book. If Lunacy is the &quot;deep down ancestral fear of the wolf at the door&quot; then I think it should apply <i>when they are at the door</i> and not just later after they'e left.<br /> <br /> Again, if you want to run your game that way you can with the book as written, but to me it seems counter-intuitive and not very thematic. Making a separate Breaking Point roll after the fact as you try and sort your supernatural encounter into a logical world view with a Lunacy roll made upon contact to determine exactly what variety of lizard-brain fight or flight you are afflicted with makes much more sense to me.<br /> <br /> Charlaquin: That is certainly true from the character's point of view, if that's what was meant. I still find it weird that this is the only specific time that's mentioned as a repeatable phenomena in the book, where elsewhere it's just storyteller-feat. Also, if it is truly &quot;random&quot; that dramatically failing a Lunacy check can turn you wolf-blooded then it shouldn't be simultaneously &quot;certain.&quot; Sometimes dramatically failing should do something else, in that case.<br /> <br /> A second your opinion on not rolling every NPC lunacy check, though. It's tiresome in groups and depending on the game and characters you get I find it bogs things down when &quot;averaging out&quot; the Lunacy reaction works just as well. The old WtF just had a straight comparison of Lunacy level to willpower that worked as a serviceable shorthand and I honestly don't know why they felt the need to change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:36:02-07:00","id":681541,"title":"","content":"Bingo. What the book presents is two methods for determining the likelihood of the exact same event. I hesitate to call anything but the lunacy roll a &quot;system&quot; at all, given that it's just carte blanch for storytellers anyone a wolfblooded they want, plus backstory fodder for players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:43:06-07:00","id":681592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681529#post681529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nofather: But aren't some of the Lunacy conditions, particularly for failure, still things like running away screaming and fainting spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets avoid hyperbole. There's Atavism, which makes someone lash out to attack the source of Lunacy or anything that stresses them. Delusion, which makes them run away from anything supernatural or shut down into a catatonic state. Or Reception, where you're open to the spirit world in a negative sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't strike me as a very thematic thing to happen only LATER when you are in a safe place and no longer under the direct effects of Luna's touch. Frankly I think that Hunters encountering a werewolf in Garu form SHOULD suffer debilitating effects upon seeing them, unless they came prepared with some sort of Lunacy counter measures not described in the Forsaken book. If Lunacy is the &quot;deep down ancestral fear of the wolf at the door&quot; then I think it should apply <i>when they are at the door</i> and not just later after they'e left. </div> </div> </div>Hunters encountering a werewolf in gauru form suffer from the gauru's Primal Fear, detailed on page 97. They can suffer from Lunacy at the time, they can suffer from it later. If you want to have it always happen the moment they see a werewolf, that's allowed by the rules as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, if you want to run your game that way you can with the book as written, but to me it seems counter-intuitive and not very thematic. Making a separate Breaking Point roll after the fact as you try and sort your supernatural encounter into a logical world view with a Lunacy roll made upon contact to determine exactly what variety of lizard-brain fight or flight you are afflicted with makes much more sense to me. </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of reasons for Lunacy to occur after the fact. Victims of surprise. Victims of one of the many mind-affecting powers of werewolves. People who were ready for a fight with a monster but not with the power of it. A werewolf isn't always going to come to the door and wait for you to let it in. Think of it as a supernatural post traumatic stress disorder, if you can't imagine any reason why people wouldn't fly into a rage when confronted by a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2015, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:53:46-07:00","id":681602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681529#post681529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nofather: But aren't some of the Lunacy conditions, particularly for failure, still things like running away screaming and fainting spells? That doesn't strike me as a very thematic thing to happen only LATER when you are in a safe place and no longer under the direct effects of Luna's touch. Frankly I think that Hunters encountering a werewolf in Garu form SHOULD suffer debilitating effects upon seeing them, unless they came prepared with some sort of Lunacy counter measures not described in the Forsaken book. If Lunacy is the &quot;deep down ancestral fear of the wolf at the door&quot; then I think it should apply <i>when they are at the door</i> and not just later after they'e left.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. They're forced to use Down and Dirty combat. And even if they've taken sufficient measures to combat the werewolf that they would be considered more than a &quot;lesser foe&quot; to a werewolf in Gauru form, they <i>still</i> can't add their Athletics (or other relevant Skill) to Defense against it. That's not what Lunacy is, though. Think about it like a horror movie. When the werewolf is right there in front of the main characters, none of them try to deny what they're seeing. They don't really have time to try to rationalize it, all they can do is run, hide, or fight. It's not until later, when they're not face to face with an eight foot killing machine that they start to say things like &quot;I don't know what I saw&quot; or &quot;It had to have been a bear, right?&quot; And that's when they start making stupid decisions like &quot;we've got to find whatever did this and put it down!&quot; or seeing weird shit, or getting jumpy about little things. That's what Lunacy is. Lunacy is the fear of the wolf at the door, not the wolf inside your house. It comes from knowing there's a big bad wolf out there somewhere that wants to eat you up, not from staring into the jaws of death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681529#post681529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if you want to run your game that way you can with the book as written, but to me it seems counter-intuitive and not very thematic. Making a separate Breaking Point roll after the fact as you try and sort your supernatural encounter into a logical world view with a Lunacy roll made upon contact to determine exactly what variety of lizard-brain fight or flight you are afflicted with makes much more sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only <i>can</i> you run it nofather's way with the book as written, that <i>is</i> the way the book is written, and you <i>can</i> run it your way if you so chose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681529#post681529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin: That is certainly true from the character's point of view, if that's what was meant. I still find it weird that this is the only specific time that's mentioned as a repeatable phenomena in the book, where elsewhere it's just storyteller-feat. Also, if it is truly &quot;random&quot; that dramatically failing a Lunacy check can turn you wolf-blooded then it shouldn't be simultaneously &quot;certain.&quot; Sometimes dramatically failing should do something else, in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not repeatable from an in-character point of view. There is a consistent mechanic for randomly determining out-of-character when it happens, and the characters, not being privy to the nature of the mechanics, only perceive the randomness. Add to that the fact that humans can become wolf-blooded by pure ST fiat, which also looks random to the characters, since they don't know there is such thing as an ST, and can't be consistently linked to a common factor. Now keep in mind that the characters don't know there's any difference between these mechanically-determined Adoptions and the fiat-determined Adoptions, and you can begin to understand why the Uratha have no idea what causes them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681529#post681529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A second your opinion on not rolling every NPC lunacy check, though. It's tiresome in groups and depending on the game and characters you get I find it bogs things down when &quot;averaging out&quot; the Lunacy reaction works just as well. The old WtF just had a straight comparison of Lunacy level to willpower that worked as a serviceable shorthand and I honestly don't know why they felt the need to change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token, why would they have felt the need to keep it the same? It was an awkward mechanic that didn't fit in very well with the rest of the system. Besides that, the bar for being able to remember what happened correctly was really low, which was not very verisimilar with the way Lunacy was presented as a tool to help ensure the herd does not know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:41:50-07:00","id":681688,"title":"","content":"Okay I think maybe I'm parsing out my problem here: in the original WtF &quot;Lunacy&quot; meant both the primal fear that made you run for your life <i>when you saw</i> a werewolf but <i>also</i> the memory loss and distortion that followed that contact. But you're saying that in WtF 2E that these are actually two different mechanics? That Lunacy is the forgetful, memory-obscuring power of Luna but that the lizard brain base fear is something else, detailed under the Gauru's Primal Fear ability?<br /> <br /> If so I apologize I've been totally misinterpreting a lot of this. Rolling to see how your memories get reshaped after seeing a werewolf is totally appropriate, I just think there should <i>also</i> be a mechanic representing the fight-or-flight instinct reaction to a werewolf in war form which it sounds like there is.<br /> <br /> I still have reservations about the Lunacy dramatic failures always resulting in wolf-bloods but that's just because I the storyteller know that it's <i>not </i>Luna's infinite caprice even if it is in the setting which I will just admit rubs me completely the wrong way. Some humans may become wolf-bloods that way in my game but I'd much rather that simply be a storyteller feat in truth without also including a hard-and-fast mechanic. At the very least it opens up some good story options involving making certain lychanthropy myths in Greek and Norse mythology &quot;true,&quot; possibly inspiring new lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:32:34-07:00","id":681717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681688#post681688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I think maybe I'm parsing out my problem here: in the original WtF &quot;Lunacy&quot; meant both the primal fear that made you run for your life <i>when you saw</i> a werewolf but <i>also</i> the memory loss and distortion that followed that contact. But you're saying that in WtF 2E that these are actually two different mechanics? That Lunacy is the forgetful, memory-obscuring power of Luna but that the lizard brain base fear is something else, detailed under the Gauru's Primal Fear ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ish. Lunacy is more than just the memory-warping, it definitely has an aspect of primal fear to it. Atavism makes you want to fight back against the source of your fear (where conventional wisdom would normally tell you that's a bad plan), Delusion makes you want to run from anything that <i>might be</i> the source of your fear, and Reception makes you intensely aware of spiritual activity around you and subsequently more vulnerable to possession. Awestruck is only caused by Lunacy when a specific Gift Facet is in effect, but it can make you beg for mercy from the source of your fear. And while the roll doesn't necessarily happen immediately, it also doesn't necessarily happen days later. It happens the next time you would otherwise be able to take a moment and process what you just experienced. That might be the next day, or it might even be in the few minutes while you're hiding and praying it loses interest in you after it catches the other guy. Just depends on what's dramatically appropriate. Either way though, Lunacy is the after-effect of an experience with a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681688#post681688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so I apologize I've been totally misinterpreting a lot of this. Rolling to see how your memories get reshaped after seeing a werewolf is totally appropriate, I just think there should <i>also</i> be a mechanic representing the fight-or-flight instinct reaction to a werewolf in war form which it sounds like there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. It's often hard to re-learn these things. That immediate fight-or-flight reaction you're looking for is better represented by the Hunter's Aspect Conditions, and to a lesser extent the Gauru form's Primal Fear ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681688#post681688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have reservations about the Lunacy dramatic failures always resulting in wolf-bloods but that's just because I the storyteller know that it's <i>not </i>Luna's infinite caprice even if it is in the setting which I will just admit rubs me completely the wrong way. Some humans may become wolf-bloods that way in my game but I'd much rather that simply be a storyteller feat in truth without also including a hard-and-fast mechanic. At the very least it opens up some good story options involving making certain lychanthropy myths in Greek and Norse mythology &quot;true,&quot; possibly inspiring new lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you're coming from. For what it's worth, it looks much more consistent on paper than it actually plays out to be in-game. Dramatic failures almost never happen organically unless there are really extreme circumstances in play, or the player opts to &quot;upgrade&quot; a normal failure to dramatic for the Beat. So Lunacy-induced Wolf-Bloodedness happens very rarely, and the circumstances that lead to it tend to be extremely varied. But, of course, if it doesn't work for you, feel free to throw it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T12:34:11-07:00","id":682271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681688#post681688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I think maybe I'm parsing out my problem here: in the original WtF &quot;Lunacy&quot; meant both the primal fear that made you run for your life <i>when you saw</i> a werewolf but <i>also</i> the memory loss and distortion that followed that contact. But you're saying that in WtF 2E that these are actually two different mechanics? That Lunacy is the forgetful, memory-obscuring power of Luna but that the lizard brain base fear is something else, detailed under the Gauru's Primal Fear ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't wrong. Lunacy includes the fight or flight part. Look at the description for failing a Lunacy breaking point on page 101, it says you lose Integrity, gain a Lunacy Condition, and either flee or panic. The Gauru &quot;Primal Fear&quot; ability is just a mechanic that reduces a lot of combat to Down and Dirty and has more to do with the power discrepancy (hence, &quot;lesser enemies&quot;) than with any fear. Myself, I think it is poorly named. Also, note that &quot;doesn't necessarily&quot; certainly doesn't imply that Lunacy breaking points usually aren't immediate, just that they don't have to be. The key phrase is &quot;dramatically appropriate&quot;. In most cases, seeing someone shift into Gauru is going to be the dramatically appropriate moment to make the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T12:45:01-07:00","id":682278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681717#post681717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see where you're coming from. For what it's worth, it looks much more consistent on paper than it actually plays out to be in-game. Dramatic failures almost never happen organically unless there are really extreme circumstances in play, or the player opts to &quot;upgrade&quot; a normal failure to dramatic for the Beat. So Lunacy-induced Wolf-Bloodedness happens very rarely, and the circumstances that lead to it tend to be extremely varied. But, of course, if it doesn't work for you, feel free to throw it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I made house rule in mine games that <i>Lunacy roll can be penlized by the number of Lethal or Aggravated damage werewolf done to the victim</i>. It leads to &quot;organic&quot; Dramatic Failures on Lunacy rolls.<br /> <br /> And so &quot;being bite by the werewolf makes you a werewolf&quot; is quasi-fact of the game ( when you equal werewolf=Wolf-Blooded in this statement ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-29-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T01:15:30-07:00","id":690961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=681717#post681717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That immediate fight-or-flight reaction you're looking for is better represented by the Hunter's Aspect Conditions, and to a lesser extent the Gauru form's Primal Fear ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>OH, </b></i>oh my my gosh that makes so much more sense now, thank you! Okay so the hunter's aspects are primal fear with flavor for auspice, which is <i>neat</i>, and Lunacy is the memory reweaving that Lunacy's blessing grants. Okay, now I'm seeing the appeal here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=682278#post682278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is why I made house rule in mine games that <i>Lunacy roll can be penlized by the number of Lethal or Aggravated damage werewolf done to the victim</i>. It leads to &quot;organic&quot; Dramatic Failures on Lunacy rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty nice house rule. I think it's a bit funny that the book suggests the exact opposite, that taking lethal; damage entitles characters to a Lunacy <i>bonus</i>. But honestly I like your version better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T01:37:40-07:00","id":690967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=690961#post690961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit funny that the book suggests the exact opposite, that taking lethal; damage entitles characters to a Lunacy <i>bonus</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get more out of lucid quarry and the main point of bonuses and penalties is to make regular success or failure more likely; it's easier to discharge regular breaking point Conditions and get down to brass tacks than it is with Lunacy Conditions and that matters when you've called the Hunt on someone for reasons that don't culminate in murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}